-- title:
--   Product of glued components restricts to (varpi) on the chart Yₙ
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, $N$ a finite type of nodes, and $C$ a chart input on $X$ with node set $N$ (so in particular data $S$, $Vc$, $\mathrm{Res}$, $\rho$, $U$, $f$, thickness $\mathrm{thick}$, base $B$, $\pi_X$, $\sigma$ with the axioms of [`V3Glue.ChartInput`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_ResolvedModelGlue.html#L291)). Assume: for every $n$ the residue-field map of $f_n$ at the marked point $xU_n$ is an isomorphism; a family of points $gRes_n : \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{thick}\,n-1) \to \mathrm{Res}_n$ is given, each lying over the vertex $\mathrm{vertex}\,n=(f_n)(xU_n)$ of $S_n$, i.e. $\rho_n(gRes_n\,k)=\mathrm{vertex}\,n$; two points $\xi_0,\xi_1$ of $X$ lie in the open $X_0$ (the complement of the marked points). Fix a node $n$, a global section $\varpi \in \Gamma(B,\mathcal O)$, and a family $F$ of ideal-sheaf data on $\mathrm{Res}_n$ indexed by $C.\mathrm{Comps} = \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_m \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{thick}\,m-1)$. Suppose that for each index $v$ the pull-back along $\iota Y_n$ (the chart map of the glued scheme) of $\mathrm{compG}\,v$ — the vanishing ideal-sheaf data of the closure of the point $\eta G\,v$ — agrees with the pull-back of $F_v$ along $g_n$, and that $\prod_v F_v$ equals the pull-back along $\rho_n \circ \sigma_n$ (that is, $\rho_n$ followed by $\sigma_n$) of the ideal sheaf data attached to the ideal $(\varpi) \subseteq \Gamma(B,\mathcal O)$. Then the pull-back along $\iota Y_n$ of $\prod_v \mathrm{compG}\,v$ equals the pull-back of that same ideal sheaf data along $\mathrm{toB}\,n = g_n$ followed by $\rho_n$ followed by $\sigma_n$.
--
--   This is the local half, on a single chart $Y_n$ of the glued scheme, of the statement that the product of the components of the special fibre of the resolved model cuts out the ideal generated by the uniformiser $\varpi$ of the base; it transports the corresponding identity on the model resolution $\mathrm{Res}_n$ across the chart map $g_n$. It feeds the verification of the `comp_prod` field in the assembly of the resolved model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3Glue_ChartInput_prod_compG_comap_iotaY_eq.lean

